		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=13217&amp;sid=da689d9e786de5221f3f25c0e5a009e0#13217"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Wed Aug 21, 2002 9:24 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=13217&amp;sid=da689d9e786de5221f3f25c0e5a009e0"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Rithnok is an honored guest at the Kindred Spirits, and as I have seen time and time again, we may not personally see eye to eye on all things, I have no doubt of his intentions within those walls and indeed within Felwithe herself. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
We of the Concordat have always left room for change within the so-called darker races, your race is not a choice for you to make. However, it is generally agreed that your profession is of your own choosing, and therefore subject to the scrutiny and judgement of your peers. It may be a fine difference, but it is a difference, and I for one will not allow Innoruuk's accursed head to rear within our halls, be it from without or within. This has always been the creed of the Concordat, and I do not foresee it's changing any time soon. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
If this offends, my apologies, but I do hope you can empathize on some level with our position. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I am deeply concerned for the Ordaen De Brell should this decision to allow those of the dark arts, namely necomancers and shadowknights within their ranks come to pass. In all of it's various forms, we have always considered those of Brell's to be amongst our staunchest of allies. My prayers are with you and yours, sir.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
 
<br />

<br />
 <i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
